Dear group,

I would like to remove a panel from my plot.  My inspiration is from this 'dirty hack' by Kohske; I am trying to do something similar to the original poster.

http://stackoverflow.com/questions/7410525/align-ggplot2-axes-using-grid

However, I can't locate the name of the panel that I wish to delete.  The following code (going from Kohske's reproducible example, provided in the link above) gives me the name of the first panel, which is "panel-2-2".  But how can I get a listing of all the panels?  grid.ls <http://grid.ls>() produces a lot of output which I am having difficulty sorting through.

