You are correct~ inserting NA into that year (1977) does work to fix
the bar width within a factor- but not across factors. Additional
issues arise (for me at least) with those NAs~ it breaks the line in
my plot with factors that have NA.

My concern with your fix is the provided data is only a ~1/20 of data,
with a variety of unbalanced observations within and between year/
treatment name (type) . Is there a way to coerce the bar with in the
whole plot within commands, not just by inserting NAs into my data?

Thanks! Sarah

