Hi all,

I´m using stat_summary2d() to visualize my data – the height of the bins (colors) should depend on a 3rd variable z. It looks something like this:

newp4 <- ggplot(data=e_au2,aes(x=xAchse,y=yAchse,z=zAchse))

newp4 + stat_summary2d(bins=5,fun=function(a) mean(a))

... and it works fine.

Now I tried to figure out whether it is possible to create a similar plot with stat_density2d(). Is there any option/new function/something else to assign a 3rd variable „z“ to define the height of the density?

Thank you for your help!

Manuel

